M1: Tags on hosts mentioning Membership or Commercial

fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, tags
| expand tag = tags
| filter contains(lower(tag), "member") or contains(lower(tag), "commercial")
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{tag}
| sort hosts desc
| limit 100


This shows which tag key and value identifies Membership, for example Portfolio:… or a product line tag, and how many hosts carry it. Watch for spelling variants, as with Claims_Modernization and Claims Modernization.

M2: The same check on OpenShift namespaces

fetch dt.entity.cloud_application_namespace
| fields id, entity.name, tags
| expand tag = tags
| filter contains(lower(tag), "member") or contains(lower(tag), "commercial")
| summarize namespaces = countDistinctExact(id), by:{tag}
| sort namespaces desc
| limit 100


M3: Applications under that tag, with names Run this after M1 shows the exact tag. Replace <TAG> with the value you find, for example portfolio:commercial markets:

fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(lower(tagStr), "<TAG>")
| expand tag = tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:") or startsWith(tag, "APPName:")
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id),
            names = arrayRemoveNulls(collectDistinct(if(startsWith(tag, "APPName:"), splitString(tag, "APPName:")[1]))),
            by:{apmid = if(startsWith(tag, "APMID:"), splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1])}
| filter isNotNull(apmid)
| sort hosts desc
